Known limitations (current prototype)
Risk scoring is rule-based (thresholds), not yet trained on historical disaster data.
No live river water-level data — flood risk is inferred from rainfall + soil moisture as a scientifically valid proxy, since most free global APIs don't expose river-gauge data.
Only 2 cities currently; architecture is designed to generalize to more regions and disaster types (see diagram in concept deck).
Next steps (if selected for pilot)
Train per-disaster-type models (flood, landslide, heatwave, wildfire) on historical datasets (EM-DAT, USGS, IBTrACS, NASA FIRMS) instead of relying solely on rule-based thresholds.
Add satellite imagery analysis (Google Earth Engine / Sentinel-2) for visual confirmation of flood extent / vegetation stress.
Partner with local government/hydrology agencies for real river-level and ground-sensor data.
Expand to additional vulnerable regions and disaster types using the same modular architecture.
